---
title: Text Video
description: Text and video with optional introductions, lists, labels and notes.
show_title: true
show_description: true
hide_table_of_contents: true
show_source: true
---

<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-4">Default styles</h2>
<p class="mx-3">These cases use the component defaults. Compare the media positions and the existing title, content and actions.</p>

<twig:block-text-video
    id="text-video-default"
    class="container my-4"
    video="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GOAEIMx39-w"
    title="Put your next project in motion"
    content="<p>Keep your team, tools and information connected.</p><p>Explore the <a href='#text-video-options'>available options</a> and choose the next step for your workspace.</p>"
    :buttons="[
        {text: 'Get started', url: '#text-video-options'},
        {text: 'Explore the guide', url: '#text-video-items'}
    ]"
/>

<twig:block-text-video
    class="container my-4"
    videoPosition="left"
    video="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GOAEIMx39-w"
    title="Keep the information close to the action"
    content="<p>The media can appear on either side of the text. The content remains first in the document and on small screens.</p>"
    :buttons="[{text: 'Review the options', url: '#text-video-options'}]"
/>

<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-5" id="text-video-options">Complete text options</h2>
<p class="mx-3">Both components accept the same text options. The templates render their contents with <code>raw</code>; ordinary text and markup use the same properties.</p>

<twig:block-text-video
    id="text-video-complete"
    class="container my-4"
    :cols="6"
    video="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GOAEIMx39-w"
    eyebrow="Workspace <strong>overview</strong>"
    title="Everything you need to work together"
    lead="<p>Turn shared information into a <em>clear next step</em>.</p>"
    content="<p>Organize your projects, share useful context and keep everyday work moving.</p>"
    :items="[
        {text: 'Keep every task in one place'},
        {text: '<strong>Share context</strong> with your team', icon: 'fa-solid fa-comments'},
        {text: 'Read the setup guide', url: '#text-video-items'},
        {text: 'Explore the available options', icon: 'fa-solid fa-arrow-right', url: '#text-video-options'}
    ]"
    badge="Available for <strong>teams</strong>"
    note="<p>Read the <a href='#text-video-items'>workspace guide</a> before configuring access.</p>"
    :buttons="[{text: 'Get started', url: '#text-video-default'}]"
/>

<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-5" id="text-video-items">Items with optional icons and links</h2>
<p class="mx-3">Each item requires <code>text</code>. Icons and outer links are optional. An item containing its own link omits <code>url</code>.</p>

<twig:block-text-video
    class="container my-4"
    video="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GOAEIMx39-w"
    title="Choose the information your audience needs"
    content="<p>Items can contain ordinary text, emphasis, paragraphs or links.</p>"
    :items="[
        {text: 'A short item without an icon or link'},
        {text: '<strong>An item with an icon</strong>', icon: 'fa-solid fa-check'},
        {text: 'An item with an outer link', url: '#text-video-options'},
        {text: 'An icon and an outer link', icon: 'fa-solid fa-book-open', url: '#text-video-options'},
        {text: '<p>Read the <a href=\'#text-video-options\'>complete guide</a> before continuing.</p>'}
    ]"
/>

<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-5">Independent label and note</h2>
<p class="mx-3">A label or a note can be used independently of the introduction and the list.</p>

<twig:block-text-video
    class="container my-4"
    video="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GOAEIMx39-w"
    title="A short availability label"
    content="<p>Describe the feature and add a status when it is useful.</p>"
    badge="Available <em>on request</em>"
/>

<twig:block-text-video
    class="container my-4"
    video="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GOAEIMx39-w"
    title="A supporting note with a link"
    content="<p>Keep the main description focused and place supporting details in a note.</p>"
    note="<p>Check the <a href='#text-video-options'>configuration guide</a>.</p><p>Workspace settings determine which options are available.</p>"
/>

<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-5">Multiple labels</h2>
<p class="mx-3">Pass a string for one badge or an array of strings for several. Each string can contain markup. The labels share the same styles and wrap onto new lines as needed.</p>

<twig:block-text-video
    class="container my-4"
    video="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GOAEIMx39-w"
    title="Connect the tools your team uses"
    content="<p>Show the available integrations without adding markup around the component.</p>"
    :badge="[
        'Project management',
        '<strong>Shared</strong> calendars',
        'Team messaging',
        'Document storage',
        'Reporting and analytics',
        'Customer support',
        'A longer integration label that wraps naturally on narrow screens'
    ]"
/>

<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-5">Long content and layout checks</h2>
<p class="mx-3">Compare long labels, notes, item text and actions on narrow screens.</p>

<twig:block-text-video
    class="container my-4"
    :cols="6"
    videoPosition="left"
    video="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GOAEIMx39-w"
    title="A longer introduction to configuration and synchronization"
    lead="An introduction that explains how the team can organize its information and coordinate the next steps."
    content="<p>The text and media share the available width and stack on small screens.</p>"
    :items="[
        {text: 'IntegrationConfigurationSynchronizationReferenceWithoutWordSeparatorsForNarrowScreenChecks', icon: 'fa-solid fa-check'},
        {text: 'A longer linked item that explains how to configure the workspace and connect the information used by your team', url: '#text-video-options'}
    ]"
    badge="A longer availability label that can wrap naturally on narrow screens"
    note="<p>Review the documentation with your team before changing the configuration of a shared workspace.</p>"
    :buttons="[{text: 'Read the complete configuration and synchronization guide', url: '#text-video-options'}]"
/>

<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-5">Video ratios and controls</h2>
<p class="mx-3">The video keeps its aspect-ratio, controls and privacy options independently of the text options.</p>

{% for ratio in ['4:3', '1:1'] %}
    <twig:block-text-video
        class="container my-4"
        video="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GOAEIMx39-w"
        aspectRatio="{{ ratio }}"
        title="Video ratio: {{ ratio }}"
        content="<p>Choose a ratio that matches the video.</p>"
    />
{% endfor %}

<twig:block-text-video
    class="container my-4"
    video="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GOAEIMx39-w"
    :showControls="false"
    :enablePrivacy="false"
    title="Explicit video player options"
    content="<p>This case disables player controls and privacy-enhanced embedding through the existing options.</p>"
/>

<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-5">Optional CSS variable overrides</h2>
<p class="mx-3">Only this case changes two variables: the heading size and the maximum content width. The cases above use the default styles.</p>

<twig:block-text-video
    class="container my-4"
    video="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GOAEIMx39-w"
    style="--text-video-title-font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2.2rem); --text-video-content-max-width: 34rem;"
    eyebrow="A focused introduction"
    title="Adjust the reading width and heading size"
    content="<p>Both components use matching variable suffixes while retaining their own defaults.</p>"
/>

<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-5">A concise introduction</h2>
<p class="mx-3">An empty description does not reserve space between the introduction and supporting note.</p>
<twig:block-text-video
    class="container my-4"
    title="Keep the next step within reach"
    lead="A short introduction can stand on its own."
    content=""
    note="Choose the information your audience needs."
    video="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GOAEIMx39-w"
/>

<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-5">Full-width background with contained content</h2>
<p class="mx-3">The root uses Bootstrap background and spacing utilities. The component creates its own responsive container.</p>
<twig:block-text-video
    id="text-video-contained"
    class="bg-body-tertiary my-0 py-4"
    :contained="true"
    eyebrow="See the workflow"
    title="Explore a shared workspace"
    content="<p>The component keeps its introduction and player on the same background.</p>"
    video="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GOAEIMx39-w"
/>
